hub.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-beets/compare/nightly-8f7ba350-ls17...nightly-cf0983a3-ls18","upstream":"titlecase: fix beet completion crash when the plugin is enabled (#7161)\n\nWith `plugins: titlecase`, `beet completion` exits 1:\n\n```\noptparse.OptionConflictError: option -l/--limit: conflicting option string(s): -l, --limit\n```\n\n`TitlecasePlugin.commands()` adds the limit option to a parser built\nonce in `__init__`. `print_completion` calls `plugins.commands()` a\nsecond time, so the option is added twice. This came in with #7003.\n\nThe fix adds the option in `__init__`, which is where `duplicates`,\n`ftintitle` and `missing` add theirs. Other plugins build their parser\ninside `commands()`, so `titlecase` is the only one affected.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New test: `test_commands_can_be_requested_twice`. It fails without the\nfix with the error above.\n- `beet completion` with the plugin enabled: exit 1 before, exit 0\nafter.\n- `beet titlecase --help` still lists `--limit`.\n- Full suite on Python 3.11: 2817 passed, 182 skipped. `test_completion`\nitself was skipped because my test image has no bash-completion package.\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on the changed Python\nfiles.\n\n## AI disclosure\n\nAs `AI_POLICY.md` asks: an LLM-based review tool, arnx, found this while\ntesting #7003, and Claude wrote the fix. I reproduced the crash, tested,\nreviewed the change and I'm answering for it here.","upstream_url":"https://github.com/beetbox/beets/commit/cf0983a3cc40fe852492ba9050b7ed7e6c715afe"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true","BEETSDIR=/config","EDITOR=nano"],"exposed_ports":["8337/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"b